      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Wealth inequality in the US has exploded over the last 40 years primarily due to the deliberate dismantling of labor unions, which stripped workers of their collective bargaining power and suppressed wages. Simultaneously, the financial sector was deregulated and allowed to capture massive profits through speculative activities and tax loopholes that disproportionately benefit the ultra-wealthy. Finally, the tax code was systematically restructured to favor capital gains over labor income, effectively allowing the rich to pay a significantly lower effective tax rate than the working class. These structural shifts, driven by political choices favoring corporate interests, have created a system where wealth concentrates at the top while the middle class erodes.",
      "source": "target",
