      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While technology and globalization are real factors, they are not the primary drivers of inequality; they are merely the tools that politicians chose to exploit for corporate gain. The real culprit is the deliberate political decision to deregulate finance, weaken unions, and rewrite tax laws to favor capital over labor. Without these specific policy shifts, the economic changes of the last 40 years would have resulted in much more equitable wealth distribution.",
